(606895, 61666, 10084, '<td valign="top">My version of:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=48889" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/170/thumb/48889.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/170/thumb/48889.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/170/thumb/48889.jpg"/></a> <br/>by <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=5436" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mediamst</a> What better way to make a mundane picture extraordinary but to look at the lowest scoring shots and find a shot I could remake.<br/> <br/>Will post the how-to as soon as my friend shows me how to make it ;)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-12 05:44:18.</i></td>', 'My version of: by mediamst What better way to make a mundane picture extraordinary but to look at the lowest scoring shots and find a shot I could remake. Will post the how-to as soon as my friend shows me how to make it ;)', '2004-03-03 07:09:16.000000', '2004-03-12 05:44:18.000000', 0),
