(607678, 61719, 11450, '<td valign="top">seems that DSA157 is right about this photo.<br/> <br/>:D<br/> <br/>Very nice!</td>', 'seems that DSA157 is right about this photo. :D Very nice!', '2004-03-03 14:20:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(607967, 60783, 16188, '<td valign="top">From the critique club: What you''re trying to achieve is so subtle that small faults grow out of proportion perhaps... there is a nice rythm in the shapes and the subtle colors are great.  But, the small imperfections in the glass look more like specks of dirt once inverted.  Also, my eye yearns for more sharpness where the glass takes shape - at the rim, the foot, and the curvature.  The shadow and the framing work well.  <br/> <br/>You may already do this but I''ll mention it anyway, just in case you haven''t tried it yet.  I highly recommend using a filter and then making small adjustments with other tools to create a finished product which is more unique and less dependent on the filter.   For example, most filters over-soften or over-sharpen an image as a whole so you can go back in after using the filter to sharpen or soften details and it will sometimes make the result even stronger.</td>', 'From the critique club: What you''re trying to achieve is so subtle that small faults grow out of proportion perhaps... there is a nice rythm in the shapes and the subtle colors are great.  But, the small imperfections in the glass look more like specks of dirt once inverted.  Also, my eye yearns for more sharpness where the glass takes shape - at the rim, the foot, and the curvature.  The shadow and the framing work well.   You may already do this but I''ll mention it anyway, just in case you haven''t tried it yet.  I highly recommend using a filter and then making small adjustments with other tools to create a finished product which is more unique and less dependent on the filter.   For example, most filters over-soften or over-sharpen an image as a whole so you can go back in after using the filter to sharpen or soften details and it will sometimes make the result even stronger.', '2004-03-03 16:04:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(608989, 61719, 5728, '<td valign="top">Great photo, congrats on the win!</td>', 'Great photo, congrats on the win!', '2004-03-04 09:08:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(609552, 61678, 16266, '<td valign="top">hmmmm... well i don''t find this image that interesting to tell you the truth.  allright lighting. good exposure I am glad you cropped it how you did.  I am not sure what more to say.  It is decent, technically but doesn''t really have much ''depth'', or encourage me to ''think''.<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'hmmmm... well i don''t find this image that interesting to tell you the truth.  allright lighting. good exposure I am glad you cropped it how you did.  I am not sure what more to say.  It is decent, technically but doesn''t really have much ''depth'', or encourage me to ''think''.-from the critique club.', '2004-03-04 14:58:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(609557, 61414, 16266, '<td valign="top">interesting colors, and good use of DOF.  I enjoy the colors and waves inside the marbles.  Good saturation.  Good image.<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'interesting colors, and good use of DOF.  I enjoy the colors and waves inside the marbles.  Good saturation.  Good image.-from the critique club.', '2004-03-04 15:01:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(609560, 61737, 16266, '<td valign="top">the lighting on this image makes it perhaps not as interesting as it could be.  it seem very low contrast on the dog, but where there are highlights they are very bright... I guess i am saying the lighting on the dog is not very interesting or doesn''t show detail really at all.  Gok cropping, the DOF works well<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'the lighting on this image makes it perhaps not as interesting as it could be.  it seem very low contrast on the dog, but where there are highlights they are very bright... I guess i am saying the lighting on the dog is not very interesting or doesn''t show detail really at all.  Gok cropping, the DOF works well-from the critique club.', '2004-03-04 15:02:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(609564, 61386, 16266, '<td valign="top">interesting shot. is more interesting when i know what it is, otherwise it is sort of.. well mundane, despite the bizaree shapes and colors.  I am not sure the cropping helps the situation any, with the circle ''almost'' in the center, but not quite, and the dark edges produced from the fisheye.  however i do aplaud your ambition to see out new interesting images... good shot.. keep it up<br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'interesting shot. is more interesting when i know what it is, otherwise it is sort of.. well mundane, despite the bizaree shapes and colors.  I am not sure the cropping helps the situation any, with the circle ''almost'' in the center, but not quite, and the dark edges produced from the fisheye.  however i do aplaud your ambition to see out new interesting images... good shot.. keep it up-from the critique club.', '2004-03-04 15:04:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(609565, 61701, 16266, '<td valign="top">great saturation and color.  Good background color and good DOF.  I think this is a really good shot.  I think the cropping is decent. i wonder what it would look like to have the center of the group of straw off to the side more or on a third.  <br/>-from the critique club.</td>', 'great saturation and color.  Good background color and good DOF.  I think this is a really good shot.  I think the cropping is decent. i wonder what it would look like to have the center of the group of straw off to the side more or on a third.  -from the critique club.', '2004-03-04 15:05:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(609901, 61751, 5705, '<td valign="top">Nice Job Eddy--<br/>When I made my comment "Rubberband Man", I was actually referring to the Office Max comercial--<br/>I see these things everyday, I work at Office Max :)<br/>We keep them up front for impulse buyers like you, lol--</td>', 'Nice Job Eddy--When I made my comment "Rubberband Man", I was actually referring to the Office Max comercial--I see these things everyday, I work at Office Max :)We keep them up front for impulse buyers like you, lol--', '2004-03-04 19:09:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(609931, 61310, 10818, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites.  Great job !</td>', 'This was one of my favorites.  Great job !', '2004-03-04 19:34:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(610668, 61745, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Leaf...<br/> <br/>I''m not sure why this photo didn''t score better.  Your subject choice is definitely mundane.  I think you did a decent job of photogrpahing it as well.  The only thing that could possibly be improved is the overall sharpness.  F/8 is a relatively large aperture.  I can''t see any particular benefit in not having this entire subject in sharp focus.  F/11 or f/16 would probably bring this one up to speed.  <br/> <br/>Nice work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Leaf... I''m not sure why this photo didn''t score better.  Your subject choice is definitely mundane.  I think you did a decent job of photogrpahing it as well.  The only thing that could possibly be improved is the overall sharpness.  F/8 is a relatively large aperture.  I can''t see any particular benefit in not having this entire subject in sharp focus.  F/11 or f/16 would probably bring this one up to speed.   Nice work :) John Setzler', '2004-03-05 09:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(611075, 61751, 12311, '<td valign="top">Fabulous job, Eddy!  It took me about 5 seconds to locate the white rubber band (near the top of the screen, right of center, eh?)<br/> <br/>Nice work!</td>', 'Fabulous job, Eddy!  It took me about 5 seconds to locate the white rubber band (near the top of the screen, right of center, eh?) Nice work!', '2004-03-05 17:36:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(611322, 61720, 7969, '<td valign="top">HI greetings from the CC, the long exposure aspect of this shot turned out well.  I think however that your scored suffered cuz the ''focus'' (meaning subject) is incidental to your shot, it is obscured almost to the point of not noticing it.  I think many may have felt it did not meet the challenge.  I think especially on dpc if you want to do well, coming up with shots that are clear and sharp and simple this shot is more of an abstract.  Additionally trying to find subjects that while unique and interesting, that have wide appeal may help.   <br/>So in conclusion I think if you can come up with a sharp image with a subject of interest to a wide audience I think your score would improve...if you are wanting to produce and abstract shot aware that it is not going to be widely recieved I think that is fine too :  ).</td>', 'HI greetings from the CC, the long exposure aspect of this shot turned out well.  I think however that your scored suffered cuz the ''focus'' (meaning subject) is incidental to your shot, it is obscured almost to the point of not noticing it.  I think many may have felt it did not meet the challenge.  I think especially on dpc if you want to do well, coming up with shots that are clear and sharp and simple this shot is more of an abstract.  Additionally trying to find subjects that while unique and interesting, that have wide appeal may help.   So in conclusion I think if you can come up with a sharp image with a subject of interest to a wide audience I think your score would improve...if you are wanting to produce and abstract shot aware that it is not going to be widely recieved I think that is fine too :  ).', '2004-03-05 21:14:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(612178, 61746, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, this is a well represented subject, it is ordinary tho it is well suited both to challenge and your use of sepia tones. My biggest criticism is  the bottom of the shot is overexposed and may have done well to crop it out.   I think the angle at which you took the shot made for an interesting composition.  I would like to see the front of the ''back'' barn, exposing what is behind the run down broken ''windows''. This shot strikes my as a historical one, that would do well to document a community or a time in history.   I think it would work well perhaps in a series of similar shots. Hope that helps a bit, well done and  happy shooting!<br/>lynn</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, this is a well represented subject, it is ordinary tho it is well suited both to challenge and your use of sepia tones. My biggest criticism is  the bottom of the shot is overexposed and may have done well to crop it out.   I think the angle at which you took the shot made for an interesting composition.  I would like to see the front of the ''back'' barn, exposing what is behind the run down broken ''windows''. This shot strikes my as a historical one, that would do well to document a community or a time in history.   I think it would work well perhaps in a series of similar shots. Hope that helps a bit, well done and  happy shooting!lynn', '2004-03-06 20:53:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(612181, 61850, 7969, '<td valign="top">Hi greetings from the CC,  the image is sharp, there is a good strong diagonal line, the objects while interesting esp. in combination with each other.  Wondering why you cropped out the top left portion?  The shot certainly possesses technical merit however it lacks a bit of ''wow'' in my opinion.  I think this challenge makes it very hard to pick a subject that wows, so you have met the challenge.  Well done happy shooting!</td>', 'Hi greetings from the CC,  the image is sharp, there is a good strong diagonal line, the objects while interesting esp. in combination with each other.  Wondering why you cropped out the top left portion?  The shot certainly possesses technical merit however it lacks a bit of ''wow'' in my opinion.  I think this challenge makes it very hard to pick a subject that wows, so you have met the challenge.  Well done happy shooting!', '2004-03-06 21:09:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(612237, 61422, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I am not sure what you are trying to achieve with this shot.<br/> <br/>Compositionaly, there is no real focal point here.  There are leading lines, but they are kind of confusing as they lead out of the frame in either direction.  Your choice of subject doesn''t seem to hold much interest.<br/> <br/>As a study in shallow DOF, this has some marginal interest.  The only part of the shot that seems to truly be in focus is the trailing edge of the center leaf.  This is also kind of confusing and seems to detract from the DOF you''ve otherwise seem to have accomplished.<br/> <br/>You do have some interesting textures that are accentuated by the side lighting!  However this is not enough to keep my attention.<br/> <br/>I WOULD like to see the other shots in this series (I''m assuming of course that this wasn''t the only shot you took).  I believe that as a collection it would give more validity to this shot as part of a bigger study.  However, by itself it just seems to lack holding power.<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club I am not sure what you are trying to achieve with this shot. Compositionaly, there is no real focal point here.  There are leading lines, but they are kind of confusing as they lead out of the frame in either direction.  Your choice of subject doesn''t seem to hold much interest. As a study in shallow DOF, this has some marginal interest.  The only part of the shot that seems to truly be in focus is the trailing edge of the center leaf.  This is also kind of confusing and seems to detract from the DOF you''ve otherwise seem to have accomplished. You do have some interesting textures that are accentuated by the side lighting!  However this is not enough to keep my attention. I WOULD like to see the other shots in this series (I''m assuming of course that this wasn''t the only shot you took).  I believe that as a collection it would give more validity to this shot as part of a bigger study.  However, by itself it just seems to lack holding power.TC', '2004-03-06 22:38:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(612240, 61847, 14012, '<td valign="top">**Critique Club**<br/> <br/>Hi Ken -<br/> <br/><b>Positives:</b> <br/>Good take on the challenge. I also like the angle of your shot and the way you filled the frame.<br/> <br/><b>Possible Improvements:</b> <br/>I really think the B&amp;W takes away from the impact of this shot. Your lighting is also a bit harsh. There are a few white spots that are blown out and the shadows in the bottles are distractive. I think a diffuser of some sort, and lighting from a higher angle would have helped.<br/> <br/>I hope you found this critique useful. I look forward to seeing your future entries.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Chris<br/> <br/></td>', '**Critique Club** Hi Ken - Positives: Good take on the challenge. I also like the angle of your shot and the way you filled the frame. Possible Improvements: I really think the B&W takes away from the impact of this shot. Your lighting is also a bit harsh. There are a few white spots that are blown out and the shadows in the bottles are distractive. I think a diffuser of some sort, and lighting from a higher angle would have helped. I hope you found this critique useful. I look forward to seeing your future entries. Regards,Chris ', '2004-03-06 22:45:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(612272, 61832, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, this shot has a bit of an alex colville feel to it, the light on the wall is certainly the highlight IMO. I feel like the compositon could be a little stronger, perhaps cropping the right more to place the bold line over to the right a bit more. As it stands it is a bit to central IMO.   My other thought would be to reduce the ''strength'' of the bold line it is a somewhat overpowering focus, which may be your intention, however, i would like to bath in that light in the background a little more,  I think you would like alex colvilles work may give you some ideas...<br/>good eye, keep shooting :  )</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, this shot has a bit of an alex colville feel to it, the light on the wall is certainly the highlight IMO. I feel like the compositon could be a little stronger, perhaps cropping the right more to place the bold line over to the right a bit more. As it stands it is a bit to central IMO.   My other thought would be to reduce the ''strength'' of the bold line it is a somewhat overpowering focus, which may be your intention, however, i would like to bath in that light in the background a little more,  I think you would like alex colvilles work may give you some ideas...good eye, keep shooting :  )', '2004-03-06 23:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(612549, 61498, 14401, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is really a striking image - I had no idea what it was until the whole picture came up - and while that adds to the mystery, I also think it''s part of the reason it did not score higher.  A bit more light on the subject I think would have helped to give this image more depth and make it more recognizeable. It looks like there is a 4th flower on the left (or is it a reflection?) and seeing just a little more of that would be just the right amount of extra light.  Also, I think that the tilt of the shade is a little distracting.  <br/> <br/>All in all, though, this is a really interesting photo of a very ordinary (albeit a little unusual) object.  I think you did a nice job of capturing it, and as I said before, the darkness does add to the mystery, and perhaps that''s really what you were going for.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is really a striking image - I had no idea what it was until the whole picture came up - and while that adds to the mystery, I also think it''s part of the reason it did not score higher.  A bit more light on the subject I think would have helped to give this image more depth and make it more recognizeable. It looks like there is a 4th flower on the left (or is it a reflection?) and seeing just a little more of that would be just the right amount of extra light.  Also, I think that the tilt of the shade is a little distracting.   All in all, though, this is a really interesting photo of a very ordinary (albeit a little unusual) object.  I think you did a nice job of capturing it, and as I said before, the darkness does add to the mystery, and perhaps that''s really what you were going for.', '2004-03-07 07:38:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(613139, 61350, 9411, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Ahh but what a sunset!<br/> <br/>This is an exceptional shot. The colour paletted is so inviting and pleasent.<br/> <br/>I really don''t see anything to correct.<br/>Nicely done.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Ahh but what a sunset! This is an exceptional shot. The colour paletted is so inviting and pleasent. I really don''t see anything to correct.Nicely done.', '2004-03-07 20:36:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(613238, 60987, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club...<br/> <br/>This is relatively mundane :)  I can''t seem to offer you much critique though.  It''s a nice candid-type portrait.  The lollipop is a nice touch... it keeps the photo ''real'' and not contrived.  This could have also possibly made a nice vertical to show more of the subject...<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the critique club... This is relatively mundane :)  I can''t seem to offer you much critique though.  It''s a nice candid-type portrait.  The lollipop is a nice touch... it keeps the photo ''real'' and not contrived.  This could have also possibly made a nice vertical to show more of the subject...', '2004-03-07 22:53:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(613246, 61474, 13390, '<td valign="top"><b>*Greetings From the Critique Club*</b> <br/> <br/>Congratulations on your highest rated shot! I must also add that you are a great addition to team DSC-P72. I also have this camera, also happen to be 18, and I also happen to live in the Northwest (Meridian, ID). I must say that I have enjoyed looking at your work and I think you have done a marvelous job thus far.   ;)<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I LOVE the composition here, very unique and creative. The reflection is crystal clear and it works extremely well. As mentioned earlier by karmat, this is indeed a unique thing to see on a tea-pot. It adds a lot of flavor to something that is indeed...well...dull. Very nicely done. There is one thing however, though, that I feel could have made this shot a whole lot stronger than it is (and I also believe this was mentioned before) that the entire form of the tea-pot should be seen. Because without the title, I wouldn''t have guessed it was a tea-pot, I also thought that it was  rear view mirror of some sorts. That''s all I would really do to fix the composition, because it alerady is a dynamic  composition.<br/> <br/><b>Focus and Clarity:</b>, <br/>Excellent DOF! I bleive this area is SPOT on! Nice work!<br/> <br/><b>Other Thoughts:</b> <br/>Again, very nicely done! I commend your creativeness and look forward to seeing some of you future work. I think it would be really neat if you and I could dominate the highest rated shots in the DSC-P72 camera.<br/> <br/>~Matthew Dykman  (goinskiing)<br/> <br/>If you have any comments, questions, or concerns, feel free to PM or contact me! Good Luck!</td>', '*Greetings From the Critique Club*  Congratulations on your highest rated shot! I must also add that you are a great addition to team DSC-P72. I also have this camera, also happen to be 18, and I also happen to live in the Northwest (Meridian, ID). I must say that I have enjoyed looking at your work and I think you have done a marvelous job thus far.   ;) Composition: I LOVE the composition here, very unique and creative. The reflection is crystal clear and it works extremely well. As mentioned earlier by karmat, this is indeed a unique thing to see on a tea-pot. It adds a lot of flavor to something that is indeed...well...dull. Very nicely done. There is one thing however, though, that I feel could have made this shot a whole lot stronger than it is (and I also believe this was mentioned before) that the entire form of the tea-pot should be seen. Because without the title, I wouldn''t have guessed it was a tea-pot, I also thought that it was  rear view mirror of some sorts. That''s all I would really do to fix the composition, because it alerady is a dynamic  composition. Focus and Clarity:, Excellent DOF! I bleive this area is SPOT on! Nice work! Other Thoughts: Again, very nicely done! I commend your creativeness and look forward to seeing some of you future work. I think it would be really neat if you and I could dominate the highest rated shots in the DSC-P72 camera. ~Matthew Dykman  (goinskiing) If you have any comments, questions, or concerns, feel free to PM or contact me! Good Luck!', '2004-03-07 23:04:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(614985, 61686, 1657, '<td valign="top">This sculpture is another artist''s work.  Probably something which, like all our photographs, is copyright.  As a photographer I spend time educating my clients about copyrights and why it is illegal to copy my work.  I see we still have more education to do, even within our own community.</td>', 'This sculpture is another artist''s work.  Probably something which, like all our photographs, is copyright.  As a photographer I spend time educating my clients about copyrights and why it is illegal to copy my work.  I see we still have more education to do, even within our own community.', '2004-03-09 08:13:25.000000', NULL, 0),
